2026-05-05T21:05:48.903Z JOY-00B0 comment.added "Real merge incident on 2026-05-05: `joy ls` failed with `duplicate field 'updated'` on a task item after a feature branch was merged into main. Two `updated:` keys appeared on adjacent lines. Confirms the failure mode: parallel `updated:` edits with enough surrounding diff are silently kept as two YAML keys instead of escalating to a Git conflict. Risk extends to any frequently-edited scalar (status, priority, effort)." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-05T21:19:32.911Z JOY-00B0 comment.added "Plan agreed 2026-05-05:\n- crates/joy-core/src/merge.rs: 3-way YAML merge on top-level mapping. Lists union-merged with dedup keys: comments by (author, date), deps/tags/capabilities by value, assignees by member. 'updated' -> max(both). All other scalars -> side with the later 'updated' wins. Driver always resolves; never emits conflict markers.\n- crates/joy-cli/src/commands/merge.rs: hidden 'joy merge driver' subcommand for git to invoke (args --base/--current/--other/--path).\n- crates/joy-core/src/init.rs: managed block in .gitattributes (analogous to existing .gitignore block) with two entries: '.joy/**/*.yaml merge=joy-yaml' and '.joy/logs/*.log merge=union' (interim, narrower than JOY-0112's Merkle-DAG design but enough to stop same-day log collisions); plus local 'git config merge.joy-yaml.{name,driver}'. Hooked into init and onboard.\n- Tests: unit tests for the merge function (clean / list-union / scalar via updated-tiebreaker / updated-max); init test for the gitattributes block.\n\nTrigger for adding the log entry to the gitattributes block: prior local-only setup on a developer machine masked the issue and let it surface in a clone today. Committing the block ships the protection to every clone." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-05T21:19:32.966Z JOY-00B0 item.status_changed "new -> in-progress" [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
2026-05-05T21:32:42.635Z JOY-00B0 comment.added "[x] crates/joy-core/src/merge.rs added: 3-way YAML merge on the AST (serde_yaml_ng::Value), recursive on mappings, set-merge on sequences with stable identity per path (comments by (author, date), assignees by member, others by value). Tiebreaker for genuine scalar conflicts is the side with the later top-level 'updated' (defaults to theirs when no signal). 12 unit tests covering duplicate-updated, scalar tiebreaker, list union, list 3-way removal, missing-field, nested mapping, JOYCRYPT detection.\n[x] crates/joy-cli/src/commands/merge.rs added: hidden 'joy merge driver' subcommand (--base/--current/--other/--path/--ours-rev/--theirs-rev). Reads bytes; if any side is a JOYCRYPT blob -> never merges, picks the side with the later git commit timestamp via 'git log -1 --format=%ct', defaulting to theirs. Plaintext path delegates to merge_yaml_doc.\n[x] crates/joy-core/src/init.rs: managed block in .gitattributes registering merge=joy-yaml on .joy/items/.../milestones/.../releases/.../ai/agents/.../ai/jobs/*.yaml + project.yaml + config.defaults.yaml, plus merge=union on .joy/logs/*.log (interim until JOY-0112). Local 'git config merge.joy-yaml.{name,driver}' set on init AND onboard, since git-config doesn't travel through clone. 3 new tests: gitattributes block presence, no duplication on re-run, git-config registration with %X/%Y placeholders.\n[x] Workspace tests: 319 + 88 + 2 = 409 passing. cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings clean.\n\nOpen: end-to-end real-git-merge integration test (using bats or equivalent) is deferred; relying on unit tests for now. Awaiting explicit OK to commit." [ai:claude@joy delegated-by:horst.schwarz@joydev.com]
